LibIPC: bound window-portal sends so a stalled peer cannot freeze the UI

The GUI thread writes WindowServer messages inline with event handling. If
LibWM stops draining that socket, a blocking write freezes the application,
and because the same thread also dispatches Wayland events, the compositor's
queue to the client fills too: neither side can recover.

Make both ends of the window portal non-blocking and give asynchronous sends
a one-second budget. If the peer is already known to be wedged, drop further
updates immediately instead of spending the timeout on each one. Sync sends
keep waiting because their callers MUST() the result.

